# Installed by bonesinfra
#
# Requires sudo 1.9.10+ (command line argument matching with POSIX extended
# regular expressions). Sudoers regexes must start with '^' and end with '$';
# sudo matches the anchored expression against the command line arguments.
#
# Trust model: this rule assumes a SINGLE OPERATOR owns every project on this
# host. The shared `deploy_user` account (default: deploy) is granted passwordless
# sudo for exactly two anchored argument forms of the root-owned BonesRemote
# binary. Any compromise of that account, or of any SSH key authorized for it,
# can deploy every project on the host.
#
# This rule is NOT a tenant-isolation boundary. Scoping the site identifier is
# insufficient while all projects still share the same Unix account and the
# same authorized_keys file, because a key authenticated as `deploy` can
# still target any project. To support multiple operators or
# tenants on one host, provision a separate deploy identity (Unix account +
# authorized_keys) per project and scope each sudoers rule to that identity
# before relying on the per-site split.
#
# The anchored patterns allow exactly `config sync --site <site>` and
# `deploy --site <site>` where <site> is lowercase ASCII letters, digits, and
# hyphens. Every other
# BonesRemote subcommand, optional deploy argument,
# reordered argument, and trailing argument is rejected by sudo. BonesRemote
# revalidates the site identifier and rejects reserved names after exec.
{{ deploy_user }} ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: {{ bonesremote_path }} ^config sync --site [a-z0-9-]+$, {{ bonesremote_path }} ^deploy --site [a-z0-9-]+$
